# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party / copyrighted source literature.
# back-end/documents/ holds published journal articles, patient guides, and
# other third-party PDFs used only as local RAG source material for
# ingest.py. These are not ours to redistribute via git history — keep them
# out of the repo and provision them separately at deploy time (e.g. a
# private bucket or volume). ingest.py reads them from disk; nothing else
# depends on them being version-controlled.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
back-end/documents/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Eval outputs derived from the above documents.
# DeepEval's Synthesizer generates goldens *from* back-end/documents/*.pdf,
# and the RAGAS runner's result CSVs embed verbatim retrieved_context chunks
# pulled from those same PDFs — both can carry copyrighted excerpts and are
# regeneratable, so neither belongs in git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
back-end/evals/**/generated/
back-end/evals/**/results/
back-end/evals/**/*.cache/
.ragas_cache/

# flagged_records.json re-embeds retrieved_context chunks filtered straight
# out of RAGAS_Baseline.csv (see above) -- same copyrighted-excerpt concern,
# and it's regenerated by load_flagged_records.py. The .sqlite files are
# TruLens's own local run databases, also regenerated each run.
# Every CSV in this folder is scored output carrying the same context
# excerpts (via the reasoning columns) and is regenerated by trulens_debug.py
# -- globbed rather than named one by one, so recheck runs writing new files
# (trulens_semantic_recheck_results.csv and friends) are covered without
# another exact-name entry each time. Nothing here is a checked-in input:
# the tracked files in this folder are only .py/.md/.txt.
back-end/evals/TruLens/flagged_records.json
back-end/evals/TruLens/*.csv
back-end/evals/TruLens/*.sqlite
